isions, and the current workspace are leads; no team channels, internal sites, private repositories, or owner identities were supplied or verified. Store any sensitive locator only in an authorized private store, never KNOWLEDGE/. [Interaction and state]: Agents and API clients act through HTTP; X-Actor is unverified caller input; requesters receive notifications; shared ticket, audit and outbox state belongs to the service and persists only when DATA_FILE is configured. Existing documentation provides no user sessions, authentication, per-user hiding, or multi-process write coordination; the default adds none, ruling out claims of authenticated attribution or new access controls. [Visibility]: Intake is visible in this result now; the implemented outcome would be visible in the isolated checkout at final return and in a deployed target only after release."
